=== day
n: 7
title: Make the page react
subtitle: The DOM and events
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: js | js | app.js
file: app.js = js
refs: @page, helpers.js, data.js

--- intro
Until now your JavaScript ran once and printed to the Console. Today the page **reacts**. You build the show cards with JavaScript, filter them while someone types, and add a watchlist called **My List** that is still there after a reload.

You work in one file, **app.js**. The page itself, the styles and two small files are ready. Open the read-only tabs above the code box to look at them:

- **data.js** holds `shows`, the 12 shows you know.
- **helpers.js** has functions you already know, like `ratingLabel`, `yearsLabel` and `searchByName`.

Your code grows from step to step: each step starts with your code from the step before.

